# Autonomous execution

Gary explicitly authorized autonomous routine work within his requested tasks.
Do not repeatedly ask him to approve necessary reversible edits, local builds,
tests or already-authorized merges. For the artist discography task he permits
merging after successful runtime verification without waiting for CI.

Inspect the execution policy before proposing any approval request. If a prompt
category is disabled, do not ask for that escalation or suggest conversational
consent can enable it. Continue with a materially safer permitted alternative.
If completion is genuinely blocked, state the actual restriction and the exact
work left unverified; do not claim a denied request was shown to Gary.

Mandatory system/tool approvals and restrictions still apply. Do not bypass
them, broaden this instruction into unrelated actions, or infer authorization
to send messages or publish externally from this routine-development preference.
